IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc6-builders`

-- ccc6-voyeurism.l4 -- s 162 (Voyeurism) and s 162.1 (Publication, etc., of an intimate image without consent).
-- An offence function answers JUST TRUE when every element is met and NOTHING otherwise (fork F1); a "public good" defence answers JUST TRUE when its two conditions hold and
-- JUST FALSE ("this section gives no defence on these facts") when they do not (fork F3). The s 787(1) penalty for the summary-conviction limb is an input (another part).

§ `s 162 Voyeurism`

DECLARE `s 162(1) what the person did` IS ONE OF
    `s 162(1) observed, including by mechanical or electronic means`
    `s 162(1) made a visual recording of`
    `s 162(1) neither`

-- src:3154 | Voyeurism
-- src:3155 | 162 (1) Every one commits an offence who, surreptitiously, observes — including by mechanical or electronic means — or makes a visual recording of a person who is in circumstances that give rise to a reasonable expectation of privacy, if
-- src:3156 | (a) the person is in a place in which a person can reasonably be expected to be nude or nearly nude, to expose their sexual organs or to be engaged in explicit sexual activity;
-- src:3157 | (b) the person is nude, is nearly nude, is exposing their sexual organs, or is engaged in explicit sexual activity, and the observation or recording is done for the purpose of observing or recording a person in such a state or engaged in such an activity; or
-- src:3158 | (c) the observation or recording is done for a sexual purpose.
@ref Criminal Code s 162(1) (src:3154-3158)
GIVEN `what the person did to the other person` IS A `s 162(1) what the person did`
      `the person did it surreptitiously` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person was in circumstances that give rise to a reasonable expectation of privacy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person was in a place in which a person can reasonably be expected to be nude or nearly nude, to expose their sexual organs or to be engaged in explicit sexual activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person was nude, nearly nude, exposing their sexual organs, or engaged in explicit sexual activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the observation or recording was done for the purpose of observing or recording a person in such a state or engaged in such an activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the observation or recording was done for a sexual purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 162(1) the conduct is the offence of voyeurism` MEANS
    IF    NOT (`what the person did to the other person` EQUALS `s 162(1) neither`)
      AND `the person did it surreptitiously`
      AND `the other person was in circumstances that give rise to a reasonable expectation of privacy`
      AND (   `the other person was in a place in which a person can reasonably be expected to be nude or nearly nude, to expose their sexual organs or to be engaged in explicit sexual activity`
           OR (   `the other person was nude, nearly nude, exposing their sexual organs, or engaged in explicit sexual activity`
              AND `the observation or recording was done for the purpose of observing or recording a person in such a state or engaged in such an activity`)
           OR `the observation or recording was done for a sexual purpose`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every one commits an offence who, surreptitiously, observes — including by mechanical or electronic means — or makes a visual recording of a person who is in circumstances that give rise to a reasonable expectation of privacy, if (a) ... (b) ... or (c)"

DECLARE `s 162(2) kind of recording` IS ONE OF
    `s 162(2) a photographic recording`
    `s 162(2) a film recording`
    `s 162(2) a video recording`
    `s 162(2) another recording made by any means`
    `s 162(2) something that is not a recording`

-- src:3159 | Definition of visual recording
-- src:3160 | (2) In this section, visual recording includes a photographic, film or video recording made by any means.
@ref Criminal Code s 162(2) (src:3159-3160)
GIVEN `the kind of recording` IS A `s 162(2) kind of recording`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 162(2) visual recording` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind of recording`
    WHEN `s 162(2) a photographic recording` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 162(2) a film recording` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 162(2) a video recording` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 162(2) another recording made by any means` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "visual recording includes a photographic, film or video recording made by any means"
    WHEN `s 162(2) something that is not a recording` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "visual recording includes"

-- (3) "Paragraphs (1)(a) and (1)(b) do not apply to a peace officer who, under the authority of a warrant issued under section 487.01, is carrying out any activity referred to in those paragraphs."
-- The function says whether the paragraphs apply to the person: JUST FALSE for the officer, and NOTHING for anyone else (the subsection is silent about them).
-- src:3161 | Exemption
-- src:3162 | (3) Paragraphs (1)(a) and (b) do not apply to a peace officer who, under the authority of a warrant issued under section 487.01, is carrying out any activity referred to in those paragraphs.
@ref Criminal Code s 162(3) (src:3161-3162)
GIVEN `s 2 peace officer: the person is a peace officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person acts under the authority of a warrant issued under section 487.01` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is carrying out an activity referred to in paragraphs (1)(a) or (1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 162(3) paragraphs (1)(a) and (1)(b) apply to the person` MEANS
    IF    `s 2 peace officer: the person is a peace officer` EQUALS JUST TRUE
      AND `the person acts under the authority of a warrant issued under section 487.01`
      AND `the person is carrying out an activity referred to in paragraphs (1)(a) or (1)(b)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraphs (1)(a) and (b) do not apply to a peace officer who, under the authority of a warrant issued under section 487.01, is carrying out any activity referred to in those paragraphs"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "do not apply to a peace officer who, under the authority of a warrant issued under section 487.01"

DECLARE `s 162(4) what the person did with the recording` IS ONE OF
    `s 162(4) prints`
    `s 162(4) copies`
    `s 162(4) publishes`
    `s 162(4) distributes`
    `s 162(4) circulates`
    `s 162(4) sells`
    `s 162(4) advertises`
    `s 162(4) makes available`
    `s 162(4) has the recording in possession for the purpose of printing, copying, publishing, distributing, circulating, selling or advertising it or making it available`
    `s 162(4) none of those`

-- src:3163 | Printing, publication, etc., of voyeuristic recordings
-- src:3164 | (4) Every one commits an offence who, knowing that a recording was obtained by the commission of an offence under subsection (1), prints, copies, publishes, distributes, circulates, sells, advertises or makes available the recording, or has the recording in his or her possession for the purpose of printing, copying, publishing, distributing, circulating, selling or advertising it or making it available.
@ref Criminal Code s 162(4) (src:3163-3164)
GIVEN `the person knew that the recording was obtained by the commission of an offence under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what the person did with the recording` IS A `s 162(4) what the person did with the recording`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 162(4) the conduct is the offence of printing, publishing, etc. a voyeuristic recording` MEANS
    IF    `the person knew that the recording was obtained by the commission of an offence under subsection (1)`
      AND NOT (`what the person did with the recording` EQUALS `s 162(4) none of those`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every one commits an offence who, knowing that a recording was obtained by the commission of an offence under subsection (1), prints, copies, publishes, distributes, circulates, sells, advertises or makes available the recording, or has the recording in his or her possession for the purpose of printing, copying, publishing, distributing, circulating, selling or advertising it or making it available"

-- src:3165 | Punishment
-- src:3166 | (5) Every one who commits an offence under subsection (1) or (4)
-- src:3167 | (a) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years; or
-- src:3168 | (b) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 162(5) (src:3165-3168)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 162(5)(a) the punishment on indictment` MEANS
    Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref Criminal Code s 162(5)(b) (src:3168)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 162(5)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS
    `ss 150 to 182 the punishment on summary conviction that s 787(1) fixes` `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

@ref Criminal Code s 162(5) (src:3165-3168)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 162 the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:3169 | Defence
-- src:3170 | (6) No person shall be convicted of an offence under this section if the acts that are alleged to constitute the offence serve the public good and do not extend beyond what serves the public good.
@ref Criminal Code s 162(6) (src:3169-3170)
GIVEN `the acts alleged to constitute the offence serve the public good` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the acts alleged do not extend beyond what serves the public good` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 162(6) section 162 gives a defence of public good` MEANS
    IF `the acts alleged to constitute the offence serve the public good` AND `the acts alleged do not extend beyond what serves the public good`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person shall be convicted of an offence under this section if the acts that are alleged to constitute the offence serve the public good and do not extend beyond what serves the public good"

DECLARE `s 162(7) the question` IS ONE OF
    `s 162(7) whether an act serves the public good`
    `s 162(7) whether there is evidence that the act alleged goes beyond what serves the public good`
    `s 162(7) whether the act does or does not extend beyond what serves the public good`
    `s 162(7) another question`

-- src:3171 | Question of law, motives
-- src:3172 | (7) For the purposes of subsection (6),
-- src:3173 | (a) it is a question of law whether an act serves the public good and whether there is evidence that the act alleged goes beyond what serves the public good, but it is a question of fact whether the act does or does not extend beyond what serves the public good; and
-- src:3174 | (b) the motives of an accused are irrelevant.
@ref Criminal Code s 162(7) (src:3171-3174)
GIVEN question IS A `s 162(7) the question`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 162(7)(a) the question is a question of law` MEANS
    CONSIDER question
    WHEN `s 162(7) whether an act serves the public good` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 162(7) whether there is evidence that the act alleged goes beyond what serves the public good` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 162(7) whether the act does or does not extend beyond what serves the public good` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but it is a question of fact whether the act does or does not extend beyond what serves the public good"
    WHEN `s 162(7) another question` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of subsection (6), (a) it is a question of law whether an act serves the public good"

@ref Criminal Code s 162(7)(b) (src:3174)
GIVEN `the matter is the motives of an accused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 162(7)(b) the motives of an accused are relevant` MEANS
    IF `the matter is the motives of an accused`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the motives of an accused are irrelevant"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (b) says nothing of any matter but the accused's motives

§ `s 162.1 Publication, etc., of an intimate image without consent`

-- (2) "intimate image means (a) a visual recording ... (i) ... (ii) ... and (iii) ...; or (b) a visual representation ... that shows an identifiable person who is depicted as nude ..., if the depiction is likely to be mistaken for a visual recording of that person". A "means" definition: closed.
DECLARE `s 162.1(2) what the thing is` IS ONE OF
    `s 162.1(2)(a) a visual recording of a person made by any means including a photographic, film or video recording`
    `s 162.1(2)(b) a visual representation made by any electronic or mechanical means, including by means of artificial intelligence software, that shows an identifiable person`
    `s 162.1(2) neither`

-- src:3185 | Definition of intimate image
-- src:3186 | (2) In this section, intimate image means
-- src:3187 | (a) a visual recording of a person made by any means including a photographic, film or video recording,
-- src:3188 | (i) in which the person is nude, is nearly nude, is exposing their sexual organs or is engaged in explicit sexual activity,
-- src:3189 | (ii) in respect of which, at the time of the recording, there were circumstances that gave rise to a reasonable expectation of privacy, and
-- src:3190 | (iii) in respect of which the person depicted retains a reasonable expectation of privacy at the time the offence is committed; or
-- src:3191 | (b) a visual representation that is made by any electronic or mechanical means, including by means of artificial intelligence software, and that shows an identifiable person who is depicted as nude, as nearly nude, as exposing their sexual organs or as engaged in explicit sexual activity, if the depiction is likely to be mistaken for a visual recording of that person.
@ref Criminal Code s 162.1(2) (src:3185-3191)
GIVEN `what the thing is` IS A `s 162.1(2) what the thing is`
      `the person is nude, is nearly nude, is exposing their sexual organs or is engaged in explicit sexual activity (or, for a representation, is depicted as such)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the time of the recording there were circumstances that gave rise to a reasonable expectation of privacy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person depicted retains a reasonable expectation of privacy at the time the offence is committed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the depiction is likely to be mistaken for a visual recording of that person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 162.1(2) intimate image` MEANS
    CONSIDER `what the thing is`
    WHEN `s 162.1(2)(a) a visual recording of a person made by any means including a photographic, film or video recording` THEN
        IF    `the person is nude, is nearly nude, is exposing their sexual organs or is engaged in explicit sexual activity (or, for a representation, is depicted as such)`
          AND `at the time of the recording there were circumstances that gave rise to a reasonable expectation of privacy`
          AND `the person depicted retains a reasonable expectation of privacy at the time the offence is committed`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "intimate image means (a) a visual recording of a person made by any means including a photographic, film or video recording, (i) in which the person is nude, is nearly nude, is exposing their sexual organs or is engaged in explicit sexual activity, (ii) in respect of which, at the time of the recording, there were circumstances that gave rise to a reasonable expectation of privacy, and (iii) in respect of which the person depicted retains a reasonable expectation of privacy at the time the offence is committed"
    WHEN `s 162.1(2)(b) a visual representation made by any electronic or mechanical means, including by means of artificial intelligence software, that shows an identifiable person` THEN
        IF    `the person is nude, is nearly nude, is exposing their sexual organs or is engaged in explicit sexual activity (or, for a representation, is depicted as such)`
          AND `the depiction is likely to be mistaken for a visual recording of that person`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) a visual representation that is made by any electronic or mechanical means, including by means of artificial intelligence software, and that shows an identifiable person who is depicted as nude, as nearly nude, as exposing their sexual organs or as engaged in explicit sexual activity, if the depiction is likely to be mistaken for a visual recording of that person"
    WHEN `s 162.1(2) neither` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "intimate image means"

DECLARE `s 162.1(1) what the person did with the intimate image` IS ONE OF
    `s 162.1(1) publishes`
    `s 162.1(1) distributes`
    `s 162.1(1) transmits`
    `s 162.1(1) sells`
    `s 162.1(1) makes available`
    `s 162.1(1) advertises`
    `s 162.1(1) none of those`

-- src:3175 | Publication, etc., of an intimate image without consent
-- src:3176 | 162.1 (1) Everyone who knowingly publishes, distributes, transmits, sells, makes available or advertises an intimate image of a person knowing that the person depicted in the image did not give their consent to that conduct, or being reckless as to whether or not that person gave their consent to that conduct, is guilty
-- src:3177 | (a) of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment
-- src:3178 | (i) for a term of not more than 10 years, or
-- src:3179 | (ii) for a term of not more than 14 years if the accused knew or ought to have known that, at the time the intimate image was made, aggravated sexual assault was being, or had just been, committed against the person depicted in the image; or
-- src:3180 | (b) of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 162.1(1) (src:3175-3180)
GIVEN `the person acted knowingly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what the person did with the intimate image` IS A `s 162.1(1) what the person did with the intimate image`
      `s 162.1(2) intimate image` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person knew that the person depicted in the image did not give their consent to that conduct` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was reckless as to whether or not the person depicted gave their consent to that conduct` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 162.1(1) the conduct is the offence of publishing an intimate image without consent` MEANS
    IF    `the person acted knowingly`
      AND NOT (`what the person did with the intimate image` EQUALS `s 162.1(1) none of those`)
      AND `s 162.1(2) intimate image` EQUALS JUST TRUE
      AND (   `the person knew that the person depicted in the image did not give their consent to that conduct`
           OR `the person was reckless as to whether or not the person depicted gave their consent to that conduct`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Everyone who knowingly publishes, distributes, transmits, sells, makes available or advertises an intimate image of a person knowing that the person depicted in the image did not give their consent to that conduct, or being reckless as to whether or not that person gave their consent to that conduct, is guilty"

-- (a)(i) not more than 10 years; (a)(ii) not more than 14 years "if the accused knew or ought to have known that, at the time the intimate image was made, aggravated sexual assault was being, or had just been, committed against the person depicted in the image".
@ref Criminal Code s 162.1(1)(a) (src:3177-3179)
GIVEN `the accused knew or ought to have known that, at the time the intimate image was made, aggravated sexual assault was being, or had just been, committed against the person depicted in the image` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 162.1(1)(a) the punishment on indictment` MEANS
    Punishment OF `by indictment`
                , IF `the accused knew or ought to have known that, at the time the intimate image was made, aggravated sexual assault was being, or had just been, committed against the person depicted in the image`
                  THEN `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`
                  ELSE `imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`
                , `no imprisonment is stated`
                , `no fine is stated`
                , `no fine is stated`

@ref Criminal Code s 162.1(1)(b) (src:3180)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 162.1(1)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS
    `ss 150 to 182 the punishment on summary conviction that s 787(1) fixes` `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

@ref Criminal Code s 162.1(1) (src:3175-3180)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 162.1(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

DECLARE `s 162.1(1.1) what the person threatens to do` IS ONE OF
    `s 162.1(1.1) publish`
    `s 162.1(1.1) distribute`
    `s 162.1(1.1) transmit`
    `s 162.1(1.1) sell`
    `s 162.1(1.1) make available`
    `s 162.1(1.1) advertise`
    `s 162.1(1.1) nothing of that kind`

-- src:3181 | Threat to publish, etc.
-- src:3182 | (1.1) Everyone who, with the intent to intimidate or to be taken seriously, knowingly threatens to publish, distribute, transmit, sell, make available or advertise an intimate image of a person knowing that the person depicted in the image would not give their consent to that conduct, or being reckless as to whether or not that person would give their consent to that conduct, is
-- src:3183 | (a) guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years; or
-- src:3184 | (b) guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 162.1(1.1) (src:3181-3184)
GIVEN `the person acted with the intent to intimidate or to be taken seriously` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knowingly threatened to do it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what the person threatens to do with the intimate image` IS A `s 162.1(1.1) what the person threatens to do`
      `s 162.1(2) intimate image` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person knew that the person depicted would not give their consent to that conduct` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was reckless as to whether or not the person depicted would give their consent to that conduct` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 162.1(1.1) the conduct is the offence of threatening to publish an intimate image` MEANS
    IF    `the person acted with the intent to intimidate or to be taken seriously`
      AND `the person knowingly threatened to do it`
      AND NOT (`what the person threatens to do with the intimate image` EQUALS `s 162.1(1.1) nothing of that kind`)
      AND `s 162.1(2) intimate image` EQUALS JUST TRUE
      AND (   `the person knew that the person depicted would not give their consent to that conduct`
           OR `the person was reckless as to whether or not the person depicted would give their consent to that conduct`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Everyone who, with the intent to intimidate or to be taken seriously, knowingly threatens to publish, distribute, transmit, sell, make available or advertise an intimate image of a person knowing that the person depicted in the image would not give their consent to that conduct, or being reckless as to whether or not that person would give their consent to that conduct, is"

@ref Criminal Code s 162.1(1.1)(a) (src:3183)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 162.1(1.1)(a) the punishment on indictment` MEANS
    Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref Criminal Code s 162.1(1.1)(b) (src:3184)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 162.1(1.1)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS
    `ss 150 to 182 the punishment on summary conviction that s 787(1) fixes` `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

@ref Criminal Code s 162.1(1.1) (src:3181-3184)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 162.1(1.1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:3192 | Defence
-- src:3193 | (3) No person shall be convicted of an offence under this section if the conduct that forms the subject-matter of the charge serves the public good and does not extend beyond what serves the public good.
@ref Criminal Code s 162.1(3) (src:3192-3193)
GIVEN `the conduct that forms the subject-matter of the charge serves the public good` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conduct does not extend beyond what serves the public good` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 162.1(3) section 162.1 gives a defence of public good` MEANS
    IF `the conduct that forms the subject-matter of the charge serves the public good` AND `the conduct does not extend beyond what serves the public good`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person shall be convicted of an offence under this section if the conduct that forms the subject-matter of the charge serves the public good and does not extend beyond what serves the public good"

DECLARE `s 162.1(4) the question` IS ONE OF
    `s 162.1(4) whether the conduct serves the public good`
    `s 162.1(4) whether there is evidence that the conduct alleged goes beyond what serves the public good`
    `s 162.1(4) whether the conduct does or does not extend beyond what serves the public good`
    `s 162.1(4) another question`

-- src:3194 | Question of fact and law, motives
-- src:3195 | (4) For the purposes of subsection (3),
-- src:3196 | (a) it is a question of law whether the conduct serves the public good and whether there is evidence that the conduct alleged goes beyond what serves the public good, but it is a question of fact whether the conduct does or does not extend beyond what serves the public good; and
-- src:3197 | (b) the motives of an accused are irrelevant.
@ref Criminal Code s 162.1(4) (src:3194-3197)
GIVEN question IS A `s 162.1(4) the question`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 162.1(4)(a) the question is a question of law` MEANS
    CONSIDER question
    WHEN `s 162.1(4) whether the conduct serves the public good` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 162.1(4) whether there is evidence that the conduct alleged goes beyond what serves the public good` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 162.1(4) whether the conduct does or does not extend beyond what serves the public good` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but it is a question of fact whether the conduct does or does not extend beyond what serves the public good"
    WHEN `s 162.1(4) another question` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of subsection (3), (a) it is a question of law whether the conduct serves the public good"

@ref Criminal Code s 162.1(4)(b) (src:3197)
GIVEN `the matter is the motives of an accused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 162.1(4)(b) the motives of an accused are relevant` MEANS
    IF `the matter is the motives of an accused`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the motives of an accused are irrelevant"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (b) says nothing of any matter but the accused's motives
